# Draft kk: Allow tessellation, geometry and heap prepasses to overlap fragment work behind MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow2
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46525 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Allow tessellation, geometry and heap prepasses to overlap fragment work behind MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow2

Under MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow, render encoders still end with MTL_STAGE_DISPATCH in beforeStages, stalling mid-pass tessellation, geometry pre-rasterization, and geometry-heap reset compute encoders behind earlier fragment work even though they only write vertex-consumed buffers.

This adds MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow2 (off by default, implies narrow):

Render encoders ending for a tessellation, geometry-shader, or heap-reset split (with no fragment wait pending and no queued post-render writes) release MTL_STAGE_DISPATCH and set frag_open.
The prepass compute encoder waits only VERTEX | OBJECTS | MESH -> DISPATCH and clears only vertex waits on completion.
Any non-prepass compute encoder opened while frag_open is set (and the first compute encoder of each command buffer) waits ALL -> DISPATCH with device visibility and clears frag_open once real compute work ends ALL -> ALL.
Pending timestamp resolves flush frag_open through a forced 1-thread compute write before calling resolveCounterHeap.

Depends on !46468, !46472, and !46524.
